WEBVTT

00:04:00.444 --> 00:04:02.738
And the Starship vehicle itself

00:04:02.738 --> 00:04:06.534
will be able to launch
over 100 metric tons of payload

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:08.077
to Earth orbit,

00:04:08.077 --> 00:04:09.495
to the surface of the Moon,

00:04:09.495 --> 00:04:10.830
to the surface of Mars

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:11.872
and even beyond.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.251
Like, 100 metric tons of payload.

00:04:15.459 --> 00:04:16.460
Like, that’s crazy.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.586
That is a crazy number

00:04:17.586 --> 00:04:20.506
that we would never
have been discussing a while ago

00:04:20.506 --> 00:04:22.091
because in spaceflight,

00:04:22.091 --> 00:04:24.302
we are always trying
to reduce mass, right?

00:04:24.302 --> 00:04:25.970
Miniaturize your components,

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:28.389
have your instruments
be as lightweight as possible

00:04:28.389 --> 00:04:30.349
because of the mass and cost constraints.